        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Ours wins everywhere except diversity.",
          "rect": [
            80,
            420,
            800,
            40
          ],
          "size": 28,
          "color": "#C00000"
        }
      ],
      "speech": "Does it work beyond cherry-picks? Hidden overlays, PASCAL VOC subjects, four styles, 15 minutes on one A100 each. The baseline is what the paper calls vanilla SDXL score distillation, so read it as an ablation, not a rival method. Green is ours: better prompt match, aesthetics, and independence, a soft score we made up where each image has to match its own prompt more than the other four, and vice versa. We lose on diversity, since we add constraints. Dream targets also beat 4000 plain score distillation steps on aesthetics. Honestly, style and prompt mattered more than our variants, and we never compared against Visual Anagrams, which can't do overlays."
