      "speech": "Limits first. It's slow, minutes per illusion. And printing shifts colors: top is simulated, bottom is the photo. We never calibrated the printer, but a measured ink model would just be another differentiable arrangement. One reviewer said, quote, not good, didn't like it. Well...other people did. It won Best Demo at CVPR 2023, became a SIGGRAPH 2024 paper, and Steve Mould and Matt Parker made YouTube videos about it. Next: Peekaboo's masks were blobby. Real transparency needs real alpha, and MAGICK gets RGBA images by asking the model for green-screen backgrounds."
